New opt-in option `--statement-expression-conclusions` (also `statement-expression-conclusions = true` in a project file). With it, the conclusion of a statement expression `S; E`, such as the condition of an `assert` or `assume` statement, is used as a fact for `E` also when `S; E` occurs under a quantifier or a logical connective in an assertion, postcondition, invariant or precondition, and not only at its top. For example, `assert forall n: nat :: assume false; false` now verifies with the option. Without the option, verification is unchanged.
